course: dictionary
lesson: 3351
title: Finding meaning from context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An examiner is a person whose job is to check something carefully, most often an exam or test. The sentence «The examiner marked our papers» tells you the examiner is the person who gives the marks.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules, not by the film makers, and not by guessing.» Trained, published rules and not guessing all tell you that examiners judge fairly, using set rules.
explain: Try the check: swap in your meaning. «Ratings are decided by trained people who check things carefully by set rules.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An examiner is a person who sets or marks an exam or test.
fact: «Examiner» can also mean someone who checks something carefully, such as a driving examiner or a medical examiner.
fact: In school, examiners mark SATs, GCSEs and music exams.
fact: «Show your working for the examiner» means show how you got your answer, so the examiner can see your thinking.
fact: «The Examiner» in a newspaper name is a title, not a job.
exercise: «The examiner marked our papers.» What is an examiner? | *A person who sets or marks an exam or test | A person who sells newspapers | A child who is sitting a test | A kind of pencil
exercise: «Ratings are decided by trained examiners who follow published rules, not by guessing.» What do examiners do? | They make the films | They sing in a choir | *They judge carefully by set rules | They decide by guessing
exercise: The driving examiner sat beside Mia and made notes all the way round the block. What is the examiner's job here? | To teach Mia to drive for fun | To drive the bus | To sell Mia a new car | *To check Mia's driving and decide if she passes
test: «Show your working for the examiner.» What does the examiner want to see? | Your best handwriting | Your name at the top only | *How you worked out the answer | The answer alone
test: A medical examiner works on crime stories. What do they find out? | Where the best ice cream is | Who won the race | *How someone died | What the weather will be
exam: Which sentence uses examiner for a person who marks a test? | *The examiner read every answer carefully | We put the examiner on the table | The Examiner is sold at the corner shop | The examiner was a fast red car
